. Administering MMF in such patients could exacerbate existing kidney damage or lead to unpredictable drug exposure due to altered clearance pathways, highlighting a critical safety consideration in clinical practice [Data: Relationships (7567)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Multiple drug classes interact with 霉酚酸酯 to alter mycophenolic acid exposure\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Several drug classes demonstrate clinically relevant interactions with 霉酚酸酯 that affect the systemic exposure of its active metabolite, mycophenolic acid. Specifically, PPI类 (proton pump inhibitors), 胆汁酸螯合剂 (bile acid sequestrants), and certain antivirals are reported to increase MPA concentrations by interfering with its enterohepatic recirculation. Conversely, 环孢素 (cyclosporine), 口服抗菌药物 (oral antibacterials), and other agents reduce MPA exposure—cyclosporine by inhibiting MRP2-mediated biliary excretion of MPA glucuronide, and antibiotics likely by disrupting gut flora involved in deconjugation and reabsorption. These interactions necessitate therapeutic drug monitoring to maintain efficacy and avoid toxicity [Data: Relationships (54097, 54099, 54109, 3134)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"替丁类药物 show no significant effect on 霉酚酸AUC in studied populations\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Unlike PPIs, 替丁类药物 (H2-receptor antagonists) do not appear to significantly alter the area under the curve (AUC) of mycophenolic acid when co-administered with 霉酚酸酯. Evidence from clinical studies involving transplant patients found no notable impact of H2 blockers on MPA AUC over a 12-hour period. This distinction is important for clinicians selecting acid-suppressing therapy in transplant recipients, as H2 antagonists may be preferable to PPIs when minimizing drug interaction risk is a priority. However, the lack of effect may be context-dependent, as study populations included hospitalized, non-stable transplant patients whose complex conditions might mask subtle interactions [Data: Relationships (54103)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Pharmacokinetic indicators 霉酚酸AUC and 霉酚酸血药浓度 are key monitoring parameters\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Two key pharmacokinetic indicators—霉酚酸AUC (area under the concentration-time curve) and 霉酚酸血药浓度 (MPA blood concentration)—are directly influenced by 霉酚酸酯 and its interacting drugs. These metrics are essential for therapeutic drug monitoring (TDM) in transplant patients to ensure adequate immunosuppression without excessive toxicity. For instance, cyclosporine co-administration reduces 霉酚酸AUC compared to tacrolimus, due to its interference with biliary excretion pathways. Similarly, changes in 霉酚酸血药浓度 can result from MRP2 inhibition or alterations in enterohepatic cycling. Monitoring these indicators allows for individualized dosing adjustments [Data: Entities (14235, 14236); Relationships (4881, 3134)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"环孢素 uniquely reduces 霉酚酸血药浓度 via metabolic interference\",\n            \"explanation\": \"环孢素 (cyclosporine) exhibits a specific and mechanistically defined interaction with 霉酚酸酯, leading to decreased 霉酚酸血药浓度. This occurs because cyclosporine inhibits the MRP2 transporter, which disrupts the biliary excretion of mycophenolic acid glucuronide (MPAG). As a result, more MPAG is converted to phenolic glucuronide—a metabolite that cannot be reconverted to active MPA—thereby reducing systemic MPA exposure. In contrast, tacrolimus does not share this effect, making the choice between calcineurin inhibitors clinically significant when used with MMF [Data: Relationships (3134)].\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 7.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The community poses a high clinical impact due to the narrow therapeutic index of 霉酚酸酯, its use in vulnerable transplant populations, and the presence of multiple significant drug interactions and a clear contraindication in renal impairment.\"\n}", "refusal"